            <ArticleTitle>SUNCT syndrome associated with temporomandibular disorders: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>300-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This case report relates the association between a rare neuralgiform syndrome (SUNCT) and masticatory myofascial pain (TMD); two different diseases with different diagnosis criteria and treatments. SUNCT syndrome was treated with a balloon microcompression procedure of the trigeminal ganglion, and the myofascial pain with injections and physical therapy. The patient was without pain at a twelve-month follow-up evaluation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
